  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training of Foresters for Conservation of Hoolock gibbon in the state of Nagaland, India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will accomplish the following objectives to help conserve endangered hoolock gibbons: (1) Educate Forest Department guards on the importance of hoolock gibbons and their habitats and provide them the skills necessary to protect the species and their habitats; (2) Train Forest Department Foresters how to identify different primate species, classify them based on age and sex, and individual identification, to maintain individual histories; (3) Train Forest guards to conduct primate surveys and hoolock gibbon population estimates; (4) Give presentations on the wildlife acts, laws, and provide further insights on wildlife crimes; and, (5) Increase the acceptance and value of and ethics towards biodiversity conservation among the forest staff and community members.</narrative>
  </description>
